1. Removed unnecessary imports and dependencies that were causing the fs module error
2. Added proper mock data structure for the form
3. Simplified the component to focus on essential props
4. Added error boundary with try/catch to handle potential rendering issues
5. Removed unused props that weren't required by the component
6. Kept the useForm hook for form management
7. Added proper TypeScript types for the mock data

This should resolve the fs module error and allow the component to render properly in the preview environment. The component now has the minimum required props and mock data to function.

